sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor User as User / Android App
    participant Storage as EncryptedSharedPreferences
    participant Gateway as Spring Security Filter
    participant RateLimiter as LoginRateLimiter
    participant AuthCtrl as AuthController
    participant DB as MySQL (users table)
    participant Crypto as BCrypt / JJWT

    Note over User,Crypto: PHASE 1: USER REGISTRATION
    User->>AuthCtrl: POST /api/auth/register (username, email, password)
    AuthCtrl->>DB: Check uniqueness (username, email)
    AuthCtrl->>Crypto: Hash password via BCrypt (Cost 10)
    AuthCtrl->>DB: INSERT INTO users (storage_limit=10GB, token_version=1)
    AuthCtrl-->>User: HTTP 200 OK ("User registered successfully")

    Note over User,Crypto: PHASE 2: LOGIN & RATE LIMITING
    User->>Gateway: POST /api/auth/login (email, password)
    Gateway->>RateLimiter: Check failed attempts (< 5 in 15 mins)
    alt Attempts >= 5
        RateLimiter-->>User: HTTP 429 Too Many Requests (Account Locked 15m)
    else Attempts < 5
        Gateway->>AuthCtrl: Forward login request
        AuthCtrl->>DB: SELECT * FROM users WHERE email = ?
        AuthCtrl->>Crypto: BCrypt.checkpw(password, user.password)
        alt Password Invalid
            AuthCtrl->>RateLimiter: Increment failed attempts counter
            AuthCtrl-->>User: HTTP 401 Unauthorized ("Invalid credentials")
        else Password Valid
            AuthCtrl->>RateLimiter: Reset failed attempts counter
            AuthCtrl->>Crypto: Generate JWT (sub=email, userId, tokenVersion, exp=24h)
            AuthCtrl-->>User: HTTP 200 OK (token, username, storageLimit)
            User->>Storage: Securely persist JWT & User Details (MasterKey AES-GCM)
        end
    end

    Note over User,Crypto: PHASE 3: AUTHENTICATED API REQUESTS
    User->>Gateway: GET /api/files (Header: Authorization: Bearer <JWT>)
    Gateway->>Crypto: Verify HMAC-SHA256 signature & expiration
    Gateway->>DB: Verify token_version == user.token_version
    Gateway->>AuthCtrl: Populate SecurityContextHolder with UserPrincipal
    AuthCtrl-->>User: HTTP 200 OK (Stored Files JSON payload)

    Note over User,Crypto: PHASE 4: LOGOUT & SESSION INVALIDATION
    User->>AuthCtrl: POST /api/auth/logout (Bearer <JWT>)
    AuthCtrl->>DB: UPDATE users SET token_version = token_version + 1
    User->>Storage: Clear active & legacy preferences (Synchronous .commit())
    User-->>User: Route to LoginActivity with CLEAR_TASK
